}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/pm-multiscale#MonteCarloAlgorithm",
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "What is the Monte Carlo algorithm used for? — used to calculate equilibrium magnetic properties such as temperature-dependent magnetization by averaging over thermally accessible spin configurations"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/pm-multiscale#MonteCarloStep",
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "How is a Monte Carlo step defined? — corresponding to one attempted spin flip per lattice site on average"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/pm-multiscale#Montecarloalgorithm",
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid71"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/pm-multiscale#Montecarlostep",
