  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/pm-multiscale#MuffinTinApproximation",
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "How is the crystal potential approximated in the muffin-tin approximation? — crystal potential is spherically symmetric within non-overlapping spheres (muffin tins) centered on each atom and constant in the interstitial region"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/pm-multiscale#Muffintinapproximation",
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid73"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/pm-multiscale#MultiScaleSimulationWorkflow",
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A computational workflow that chains simulation steps across different spatial/temporal scales (e.g., DFT -> spin dynamics -> micromagnetics). Each step produces parameters consumed by the next."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "MultiScaleSimulationWorkflow"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_64963ed6_39c9_4258_85e0_6466c4b5420c"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_7d56ec24_499d_487a_af7d_a91aaa787bfe"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid74"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "MultiScaleSimulationWorkflow"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/pm-multiscale#Nanocomposite",
  "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A nanocomposite hard/soft two-phase magnet is a rigid, sortal material class central to PM multi-scale simulation; it is not expressible as any single existing magmo: class (it combines hard and soft phases at nanoscale), so a new subclass under magmo:CrystallineMagneticMaterial is required."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/pm-multiscale"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "nanocomposite"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/magnetic-material#CrystallineMagneticMaterial"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid75"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "nanocomposite"
  } ]
